    "ledger": [
      {
        "id": "E1",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Welcome Beam: a 501B open model you can own, customize, and scale",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/reflection-beam",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-18T00:01:23.012Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E2",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "It's a mixture-of-experts (MoEs) model with 501B parameters (23B active per token), supports text as input, has a context window of 1M tokens , and is released under the Apache 2.0 license.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/reflection-beam",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-18T00:01:23.012Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "It is for teams that want a frontier-scale model on their own hardware, infrastructure, or cloud, and want to customize it to their own use cases.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/reflection-beam",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-18T00:01:23.012Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Beam ships with its own dedicated open source Rust based harness that delivers the best performance from the model.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/reflection-beam",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-18T00:01:23.012Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "If you build something with Beam, then share it on the Hub for a chance to win $10,000.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/reflection-beam",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-18T00:01:23.012Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Beam is a text-only model built for long-context (1M context length) reasoning and agentic work.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/reflection-beam",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-18T00:01:23.012Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "All 256 experts stay in memory, so deployment needs the memory of a 501B model but runs at the speed of a 23B one.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/reflection-beam",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-18T00:01:23.012Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "A B200 has 180 GB of HBM3e, so two of them (360 GB) can hold the Beam weights, with little room left for activations and the KV cache.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/reflection-beam",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-18T00:01:23.012Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "You can also serve it on a full 8xB200 node, or on two B300s at 288 GB each, or even 8xRTX Pro 6000.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/reflection-beam",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-18T00:01:23.012Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Beam writes tool-call arguments inline, in its own XML-style grammar, so a bare 7 could be a number or a string.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/reflection-beam",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-18T00:01:23.012Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "A small drafter model proposes up to 15 tokens ahead, and Beam checks them all in one forward pass, so each step can accept several tokens.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/reflection-beam",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-18T00:01:23.012Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E12",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Beam is a 501B open model that you can run on your own hardware and change.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/reflection-beam",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-18T00:01:23.012Z"
      }
    ],
